<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on FOB Omaha basis carlot prices of fabricated beef cuts and on industry yields as of 1500 CST, boxed beef was generally steady on very light demand and offerings. Select and Choice rib and round cuts were steady to weak, chuck and loin cuts steady to firm. Beef trimmings were steady to firm on light to moderate demand/offerings. -- USDA</p>
<p> 108 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>  36 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>6 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     107.60	106.20	 98.68	 98.40</p>
<p>		   -0.14	  0.13	 -0.06	  0.21</p>
<p>Rib	  182.99	173.03	142.37	142.26</p>
<p>Chuck	 76.74	 75.22	 80.20	 75.34</p>
<p>Round	 93.37	 93.37	 93.82	 93.82</p>
<p>Loin	 158.08	158.85	131.93	137.41</p>
<p>Brisket     67.08	 67.08	 67.73	 67.73</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  63.30	 63.23	 63.51	 63.36</p>
<p>Flank	 67.52	 67.52	 66.39	 66.39</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
